      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017, The American Society for Clinical Pharmacology and Therapeutics.",
        "AbstractText": "Hepatic organic cation transporter 1 (OCT1) can be a determinant of drug clearance and distribution, which can impact drug exposure and response. OCT1 was shown recently to be the rate-determining step in the clearance of several drugs in humans, and thereby a mechanism of pharmacogenetic variability and drug-drug interactions (DDIs). OCT1 mediates metformin distribution to the liver (key biophase). As OCT1 modulation impacts metformin response, but not pharmacokinetics (PK), metformin DDI studies require pharmacodynamic endpoint(s) to inform rational metformin dose adjustment."
      },
